        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "45c52fe6-a67a-5bcb-989d-efb5ffeba136",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Hutchison, William K. Howard, Alma Hanlon, Florence Short, Mary Doyle\n- Films: The Golden God, Back Door to Heaven, The Thundering Herd, The Power and the Glory, Fire Over England, Johnny Come Lately\n- Roles: actor, director\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Hutchison appeared in 49 films between 1914 and 1944.\n- Charles Hutchison directed 33 films between 1915 and 1938.\n- The 1917 film The Golden God stars Charles Hutchison, Alma Hanlon, Florence Short, and Mary Doyle.\n- William K. Howard directed over 50 films from 1921 to 1946 and was considered one of Hollywood's leading directors.\n- William K. Howard's films include The Thundering Herd (1925), The Power and the Glory (1933), Fire Over England (1937), and Johnny Come Lately (1943).\n- Back Door to Heaven is a 1939 American crime drama film directed by William K. Howard.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "92548cb3-8de6-5692-a5be-56b6c7958423",
        "text": "Page: Charles Hutchison. Sentence: He appeared in 49 films between 1914 and 1944.\nPage: Charles Hutchison. Sentence: He also directed 33 films between 1915 and 1938.\nPage: William K. Howard. Sentence: Considered one of Hollywood's leading directors, he directed over 50 films from 1921 to 1946, including \"The Thundering Herd\" (1925), \"The Power and the Glory\" (1933), \"Fire Over England\" (1937), and \"Johnny Come Lately\" (1943).\nPage: The Golden God (1917 film). Sentence: The film stars Charles Hutchison, Alma Hanlon, Florence Short, and Mary Doyle.\nPage: Back Door to Heaven. Sentence: Back Door to Heaven is a 1939 American crime drama film directed by William K. Howard.",
